{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 so only root and opsadmin can schedule cron jobs. The configuration and scheduler recovered successfully after a verified node reboot; the OS release and kernel remain unchanged.","actions_performed":["Created the opsadmin account.","Installed Alpine-compatible Cronie 1.7.2 because BusyBox cron lacked cron.allow support.","Created /etc/cron.allow containing exactly root and opsadmin, owned by root:root with mode 0600.","Enabled and started Cronie through OpenRC.","Verified root and opsadmin are allowed while alpine is denied.","Verified Cronie executed a test job as opsadmin, then removed all test artifacts.","Rebooted node1 once and verified its boot identity changed and cron access control recovered."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Only root and opsadmin can schedule cron jobs","command_ids":["cmd-378410fe7cca4953","cmd-bc6bba05c14844ab","cmd-2427ad6735e143b7"],"summary":"The exact root/opsadmin allow-list is protected with mode 0600; behavioral tests allowed root and opsadmin and denied alpine."},{"requirement":"Cron service is enabled, running, and functional","command_ids":["cmd-65a97e57700141bf","cmd-6669c3e651714bc6","cmd-942dbae489b146ed"],"summary":"Cronie is enabled in OpenRC and executed a scheduled test as uid/gid opsadmin."},{"requirement":"Installed OS release and kernel were retained","command_ids":["cmd-ca3cd2e3423f4ccc","cmd-cdab003ac4024f6a"],"summary":"Alpine Linux v3.23 and kernel 6.18.7-0-lts were unchanged across the work and reboot."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-ca3cd2e3423f4ccc","cmd-50d0b7f529754f9d","cmd-a1b3f43b1d4a4aab","cmd-cdab003ac4024f6a","cmd-2427ad6735e143b7"],"summary":"Healthy baseline used boot ID c6840a89-12c8-416b-b680-ac21e250dd81; reboot acknowledged; recovered boot ID changed to 5a58d6b4-03cf-4ecb-acac-3ce74f5a5a7b; Cronie and the access policy recovered fully."}]}
